  (descr "BARE LARGE solar cell 78.55 x 38.90 x 0.21 mm, mounted END-ONLY (no bond, no carrier) on the hub array face. Body X/Y/Z CITED: ADR-049 s'Measured inputs' (78.55 x 38.90 x 0.21 mm, 30.6 cm2, ~0.5 V, ~1.2 A), reproduced by ADR-051 s1.4. ADR-052 s2.6 END-ONLY; ADR-055 D1/D3/D6 (horizontal plane, area is a DUTY CHOICE, cells on the sun-facing face). NO LANDS, measured 2026-10-08: (1) no in-repo record fixes the cell's terminal-land geometry, so any pad here would be a TODO(unverified) invention; (2) with lands present the S0 screen - gate25_check.py's LAYER-BLIND pad-box proxy - reported 5 pad-overlap pairs and 11 exact pad overlaps, ALL between a footprint on F.Cu and this cell on B.Cu (U1, U2, C_MON, D_HUB2, C_CAP2), i.e. physical non-issues on OPPOSITE copper faces, while the authority (kicad-cli pcb drc) reported courtyards_overlap 0 either way. Recommendation: make the S0 proxy layer-aware before lands are added. PLAIN PADS, NO SLOT: no routed slot and no NPTH feature (ADR-046 Option B). DNP: the array AREA is the operator's open duty choice (ADR-055 D3).")
  (tags "solar cell LARGE 78x39 hub array ADR-051 ADR-052 ADR-055 DNP END-ONLY no-slot no-lands")
